OFFICIAL-SENSITIVE

Good morning,

The Met Office has issued an amber warning for rain for Cumbria and North Lancashire,
valid from 0600 Tuesday to 1800 Wednesday. Storm Fenella response will bring 60-100 mm of rain
widely and up to 180 mm on high ground. Gusts of 60-70 mph are likely on exposed coasts
and routes.

I will join the Cumbria Resilience Forum and Lancs LRF teleconferences this afternoon.

